#!/usr/bin/env -S m9c --run
MODULE MkKeywords ;

(* MkKeywords writes the keyword reference the editor's hovers serve.

   It generates one curated paragraph per keyword into
   tools/edit/keywords.json.  The set is GATED against the lexer's own
   table in both directions.  A keyword added there without a
   paragraph here fails the build, and a paragraph for a keyword the
   lexer does not know is refused the same way.  This is the
   diagnose.md discipline, applied to the language's own vocabulary.

       tools/MkKeywords.m9            regenerate
       tools/MkKeywords.m9 --check    verify, exit 1 on drift

   (M9LIBRARY must reach corpus/: the script imports the lexer.)

   The lexer is asked, not read: every token kind whose NAME lexes
   back as that same kind is a keyword (EOF lexes as an identifier and
   so is not one).  mkkeywords.py read Lex.m9's KwName with a regular
   expression; this asks KindName and Next, the lexer's own interface.

   The JSON is written as Python's json.dumps (indent=1,
   sort_keys=True) wrote it, which the editor and the gate have read
   since the table existed: one key a line, one blank of indent, the
   keys in order.  The texts are ASCII without a quote or a backslash,
   so nothing needs escaping.  The program refuses one that would,
   rather than write broken JSON.                                     *)

IMPORT Io ;
IMPORT Lex ;
IMPORT DynStr ;
IMPORT Fmt ;
IMPORT Text ;

CONST
  Keys = [
    'AND',
    'ARRAY',
    'BEGIN',
    'BY',
    'CASE',
    'CONST',
    'DEFINITION',
    'DISPOSE',
    'DIV',
    'DO',
    'ELSE',
    'ELSIF',
    'END',
    'EXCEPT',
    'EXCEPTION',
    'EXIT',
    'FALSE',
    'FINALLY',
    'FOR',
    'FROM',
    'GRID',
    'IF',
    'IMPLEMENTATION',
    'IMPORT',
    'IN',
    'IS',
    'KEPT',
    'LINK',
    'LOOP',
    'MOD',
    'MODULE',
    'MONITOR',
    'NEW',
    'NONE',
    'NOT',
    'OF',
    'OPT',
    'OR',
    'OWN',
    'POOL',
    'PROCEDURE',
    'PTR',
    'RAISE',
    'RAISES',
    'RECORD',
    'RETURN',
    'RO',
    'SHARED',
    'SIGNAL',
    'SLICE',
    'SOME',
    'STATEFUL',
    'TASK',
    'THEN',
    'THREAD',
    'TO',
    'TRANSFER',
    'TRUE',
    'TYPE',
    'UNSAFE',
    'VAR',
    'WAIT',
    'WHILE'
  ] ;
  Docs = [
    'Boolean conjunction. Relations bind tighter than AND, and AND tighter than OR -- the corpus wrote that shape six times and the grammar followed it (report par 10).',
    'A fixed-size value array: ARRAY N OF T, with N a literal or literal CONST. Storage lives in the enclosing frame, record or module; at a call site an array lends as a SLICE.',
    "Opens a body -- a procedure's or a module's. A module body is the frame with no caller: whatever it can raise, it must handle.",
    'The step of a counted loop: FOR i := a TO b BY s DO ... END.',
    'Total dispatch. Over a scalar, arms carry literal labels (a repeated label is refused at compile time); over a CASE RECORD, every variant must have an arm or an ELSE, and pattern arms bind the payload fields.',
    'A named literal. CONSTs are untyped and adapt exactly as the literal would -- an integer fits any width it fits, a real fits F32 or F64. Allowed at module level and inside a procedure; a local may not shadow a module CONST.',
    'Opens a DEFINITION MODULE: the contract importers see -- types, procedures with their RAISES and KEPT declarations, exceptions. Everything the reviewer needs is meant to be here.',
    'Consumes an owned pointer (its name is dead afterwards, and the checker says what killed it), or releases one handle of a SHARED pointer -- the interior is freed with the last handle. A borrow or a pool-interior pointer cannot be DISPOSEd (par 4.2, 4.3).',
    'Integer division, truncating toward zero, checked: division by zero and MIN DIV -1 raise. Floats divide with /.',
    'Closes a loop header: WHILE cond DO, FOR ... DO.',
    'The remaining arm of IF or CASE.',
    'A chained condition in an IF; each condition is evaluated only if the ones above failed, so a raising guard stays behind its test.',
    "Closes every construct; a module's END repeats the module name.",
    'Opens the handler section of a body: arms name exceptions (| Io.IOError (p) : ...), binders receive the payload, an unmatched raise propagates to the caller.',
    'Declares exceptions with typed payload fields: EXCEPTION SizeError (got, want: I64). RAISES may only cite declared names.',
    'Leaves the innermost LOOP. Refused where leaving would skip cleanup or break generated control flow (across FINALLY, inside a CASE arm) -- the refusal is loud, not silent.',
    'The BOOL literal.',
    'Cleanup that runs however the block ends -- normal fall-through, RETURN, or a raise on its way out (report par 5). The C mapping is a goto chain, not setjmp.',
    'The counted loop: FOR i := a TO b [BY s] DO ... END. Bounds are integers, evaluated once.',
    'Imports names from a FOREIGN unit only: FROM cunit IMPORT Read, Write. m9c deliberately does not resolve a FROM target to an .m9 file -- there is none; M9 modules are imported whole with IMPORT and used qualified.',
    'An n-dimensional array: rank in the type (GRID 2 OF F64), shape in the value, one stride per axis. Every index is checked against its own extent; VIEW drops axes; born from Mat.Get (m, 0, 3) silently answering element (1,0) of a 2x3 matrix (report par 2.2.1).',
    'IF cond THEN ... [ELSIF ...] [ELSE ...] END. The condition must be BOOL. An IS SOME binding may stand as the whole condition.',
    'Opens an IMPLEMENTATION MODULE: the bodies behind a definition. Signatures must conform to the definition exactly.',
    'Brings a module into scope; its names are used qualified (Io.WriteLine). Imports come first in a module.',
    'Ties a pointer to its arena: PTR T IN pool names who owns the storage and so who frees it. A pool-interior pointer may not outlive its pool (par 4.3).',
    'The variant test that binds: IF x IS SOME p THEN ... END makes p the payload inside the arm. Legal only as the whole condition of IF, ELSIF or WHILE.',
    "Declared retention (par 4.1): the callee stores this parameter somewhere that outlives the call -- module state, the caller's storage, the answer. The checker computes where every store's destination escapes to and refuses an undeclared retention; the declaration composes upward the way RAISES does. The sixty-first keyword.",
    'On a foreign (FOR C) unit, after its name: what the unit links -- a library name (NetCDF links netcdf), a linker word as it is (-l:libblosc.so.1), a shim source beside the runtime (pgshim.c). m9c puts them on every flagless link, under --run and --cell; a line taken over with -- names them itself.',
    'The unconditioned loop; EXIT leaves it.',
    'Integer remainder, checked like DIV.',
    'A program: MODULE Name ; ... BEGIN ... END Name. Also the second word of DEFINITION MODULE and IMPLEMENTATION MODULE.',
    'A record whose state is guarded by one lock. Its fields are reachable only through procedures bound to it (the bare first parameter names the monitor); a bound body holds the lock for its whole extent, and WAIT releases it while sleeping (report par 6).',
    'Allocates from a pool: NEW (pool, T) one value, NEW (pool, T, n) a SLICE OF T, NEW (pool, T, n1, n2, ...) a GRID. Pool storage is defined-zero. The pool comes first -- reversing the arguments is refused by name.',
    'The absent OPT value; fits any OPT type. There is no NIL to dereference -- absence is typed.',
    'Boolean negation.',
    'Connects a former to its element: ARRAY 4 OF F64, SLICE OF CHAR, GRID 2 OF F64, CASE x OF.',
    'A value that may be absent: OPT PTR T. It cannot be read, dereferenced or selected through without IS SOME binding the present case -- the faith-based downcast made uncompilable.',
    'Boolean disjunction; binds loosest.',
    "The taking parameter mode: the argument MOVES into the callee (par 4.2), and the caller's name for it is dead afterwards. Retention by transfer, visible in the signature.",
    'An arena: allocations are carved from it and freed as one unit when it dies. Declared as a local (dies with the frame), a VAR parameter (the caller owns it), or received implicitly per call for + and string results (par 2.3). Storage is defined-zero, so an uninitialized read does not exist.',
    'Declares a procedure. The signature carries the whole contract: parameter modes (VAR, OWN, RO, KEPT), the result, RAISES, and attributes like [PURE].',
    'A pointer. PTR T from NEW (pool, T) is owned by exactly one binding unless the type says IN pool (the pool owns it) or SHARED (reference-counted).',
    'Raises a declared exception, filling its payload: RAISE SizeError (got, want). FINALLY blocks on the way out still run.',
    "The signature's failure list, checked exhaustively: every exception a body can produce -- its own RAISEs plus its callees' declared sets, minus what it handles -- must appear here. Overflow, IndexError and OutOfMemory are ambient and never declared.",
    'A record type. The CASE RECORD form declares variants with payload fields; a variant value is built with a constructor (Value.Str (x)) and taken apart only by CASE.',
    "Answers the caller. In a function every path must RETURN or RAISE -- the checker proves it. A string result is built in the CALLER's arena (par 2.3); a pool-interior pointer may not escape a pool that dies with the frame.",
    'The read-only borrow mode: the callee may read, may not write and may not lend onward as VAR -- for records and arrays too, where it is also the no-copy mode. Compose with KEPT when the borrow is retained.',
    'Reference-counted ownership: SHARED PTR T. Created explicitly -- SHARED (x) consumes the owned pointer and answers the first handle; copies count; DISPOSE releases one handle and the interior frees with the last. The count is not atomic unless the type is SHARABLE (par 6).',
    'Wakes a waiter inside a monitor.',
    'A view: SLICE OF T is {pointer, length}, every index checked. Also the sub-slice form SLICE (s, start, len) -- start and LENGTH, never an inclusive end -- and the array view SLICE (arr, start, len).',
    'The present OPT: SOME (x) wraps, and IS SOME tests-and-binds.',
    "Marks a definition whose module carries state (module variables behind the interface). Plot is the corpus' example: AddLine accumulates into a module-level figure, and the definition says so.",
    'Starts a procedure as a task: TASK (P, arg). A task is far cheaper than a THREAD and runs on the thread that starts it until it waits (stage 1 of docs/task-plan.md). The argument follows the THREAD rules -- a MONITOR, a record marked [SHARABLE], or an owned value moved in -- and a monitor may be shared by tasks and threads.',
    'Follows an IF or ELSIF condition.',
    'Starts a procedure on a new thread: THREAD (P, arg). The one argument must be SHARABLE -- a MONITOR (shared by reference, its lock is the point) or an owned value moved in. Foreign [SERIAL] procedures are serialised by an emitted per-unit monitor, so a thread reaching one waits instead of racing.',
    'The upper bound of FOR.',
    'Declared in the report (par 6) and not yet generated -- the honest state, stated.',
    'The BOOL literal.',
    'Opens a type section. Aliases chase to structure for conformance; records, monitors and opaques are nominal.',
    "Marks a unit allowed ADR and FOR-C foreign declarations. m9c --no-unsafe refuses a closure that declares one outside the trusted library directories -- the tutorial compiles strangers' code behind exactly that wall.",
    "As a parameter mode: an exclusive, mutable borrow -- the callee may write, the caller's alias is suspended, retention still needs KEPT. As a section keyword: declares variables, defined-zero.",
    'Blocks inside a monitor until SIGNAL, releasing the lock while asleep.',
    'The tested loop: WHILE cond DO ... END. An IS SOME binding may be the condition and rebinds per iteration.'
  ] ;

(* Before answers TRUE when a sorts before b, character by character. *)
PROCEDURE Before (RO a, b: STR) : BOOL =
VAR i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  i := 0 ;
  WHILE (i < Text.BLen (a)) AND (i < Text.BLen (b)) DO
    IF Text.BAt (a, i) # Text.BAt (b, i) THEN RETURN Text.BAt (a, i) < Text.BAt (b, i) END ;
    i := i + 1
  END ;
  RETURN Text.BLen (a) < Text.BLen (b)
END Before ;

(* LexerKnows answers TRUE when s is a keyword of the lexer: its kind's
   name, lexed, is that kind. *)
PROCEDURE LexerKnows (RO KEPT s: STR) : BOOL =
  (* s is KEPT because Init keeps its source.  The lexer lives no
     longer than this call, but the checker reads the heading, not the
     lifetime.
     (A copy in a scratch pool stood here until 2026-10-08, when the
     checker learned that a pool-taking callee answers into its pool
     and refused the copy into KEPT, as it refuses a frame value.) *)
VAR
  lx : Lex.Lexer ;
  t : Lex.Token ;
BEGIN
  Lex.Init (lx, s) ;
  Lex.Next (lx, t) ;
  RETURN (t.kind > 6) AND Text.Eq (Lex.KindName (t.kind), s)
END LexerKnows ;

(* Root answers the root of the repository: this file is
   ROOT/tools/MkKeywords.m9, and --run tells it its own name. *)
PROCEDURE Root (RO self: STR) : STR =
VAR i, cut, seen : I64 ;
BEGIN
  cut := -1 ;
  seen := 0 ;
  i := Text.BLen (self) - 1 ;
  WHILE (i >= 0) AND (seen < 2) DO
    IF Text.BIs (self, i, '/') THEN seen := seen + 1 ; cut := i END ;
    i := i - 1
  END ;
  IF seen = 1 THEN RETURN '.' END ;       (* tools/MkKeywords.m9 *)
  IF seen = 0 THEN RETURN '..' END ;      (* MkKeywords.m9, from tools/ *)
  RETURN SLICE (self, 0, cut)
END Root ;

(* Json answers the table as json.dumps (indent=1, sort_keys=True)
   writes it. *)
PROCEDURE Json (VAR pool: POOL) : STR =
VAR
  d : PTR DynStr.DString IN pool ;
  i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  d := DynStr.New (pool) ;
  DynStr.Append (d, '{') ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (Keys) - 1 DO
    IF i > 0 THEN DynStr.Append (d, ',') END ;
    DynStr.AppendChar (d, 0AC) ;
    DynStr.Append (d, ' "') ;
    DynStr.Append (d, Keys[i]) ;
    DynStr.Append (d, '": "') ;
    DynStr.Append (d, Docs[i]) ;
    DynStr.Append (d, '"')
  END ;
  DynStr.AppendChar (d, 0AC) ;
  DynStr.Append (d, '}') ;
  DynStr.AppendChar (d, 0AC) ;
  RETURN DynStr.ViewIn (pool, d)
END Json ;

(* NeedsEscape asks for a text JSON would have to escape: a quote, a
   backslash, a control character or anything past ASCII. *)
PROCEDURE NeedsEscape (RO s: STR) : BOOL =
VAR i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  FOR i := 0 TO Text.BLen (s) - 1 DO
    IF (Text.BIs (s, i, '"')) OR (Text.BIs (s, i, 05CC)) OR (I64 (Text.BAt (s, i)) < ORD (020C)) OR (I64 (Text.BAt (s, i)) > ORD (07EC)) THEN
      RETURN TRUE
    END
  END ;
  RETURN FALSE
END NeedsEscape ;

VAR
  pool : POOL ;
  out, text, cur, missing, extra : STR ;
  i, k, n : I64 ;
  check, bad : BOOL ;
  ok : SLICE OF BOOL ;

BEGIN
  check := (Io.ArgCount () > 1) AND Text.Eq (Io.Arg (pool, 1), '--check') ;
  out := Text.Keep (pool, Root (Io.Arg (pool, 0)) + '/tools/edit/keywords.json') ;

  (* the table's own shape: one text a key, the keys in order, nothing
     to escape *)
  bad := FALSE ;
  IF LEN (Keys) # LEN (Docs) THEN
    Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: ' + Fmt.I64Str (LEN (Keys)) + ' keys and '
                  + Fmt.I64Str (LEN (Docs)) + ' texts') ;
    Io.Halt (1)
  END ;
  FOR i := 1 TO LEN (Keys) - 1 DO
    IF NOT Before (Keys[i - 1], Keys[i]) THEN
      Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: ' + Keys[i] + ' is out of order after '
                    + Keys[i - 1] + ' (keep Keys sorted)') ;
      bad := TRUE
    END
  END ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (Docs) - 1 DO
    IF NeedsEscape (Docs[i]) THEN
      Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: the text of ' + Keys[i]
                    + ' needs JSON escaping, which this does not write') ;
      bad := TRUE
    END
  END ;
  IF bad THEN Io.Halt (1) END ;

  (* both directions against the lexer *)
  missing := '' ;
  n := 0 ;
  ok := NEW (pool, BOOL, LEN (Keys)) ;
  FOR k := 0 TO 255 DO
    IF LexerKnows (Lex.KindName (k)) THEN
      n := n + 1 ;
      i := 0 ;
      WHILE (i < LEN (Keys)) AND NOT Text.Eq (Keys[i], Lex.KindName (k)) DO
        i := i + 1
      END ;
      IF i < LEN (Keys) THEN
        ok[i] := TRUE
      ELSE
        missing := Text.Keep (pool, missing + ' ' + Lex.KindName (k))
      END
    END
  END ;
  extra := '' ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (Keys) - 1 DO
    IF NOT ok[i] THEN extra := Text.Keep (pool, extra + ' ' + Keys[i]) END
  END ;
  IF Text.BLen (missing) > 0 THEN
    Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: the lexer knows these and the table does not:'
                  + missing) ;
    Io.Halt (1)
  END ;
  IF Text.BLen (extra) > 0 THEN
    Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: the table documents these and the lexer does not:'
                  + extra) ;
    Io.Halt (1)
  END ;

  text := Json (pool) ;
  IF check THEN
    cur := '' ;
    IF Io.Exists (out) THEN
      cur := DynStr.Chars (pool, Io.ReadFileBytes (pool, out))
    END ;
    IF NOT Text.Eq (cur, text) THEN
      Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: keywords.json is stale; run tools/MkKeywords.m9') ;
      Io.Halt (1)
    END ;
    Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: ' + Fmt.I64Str (n) + ' keywords documented, none adrift')
  ELSE
    Io.WriteFile (out, text) ;
    Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: ' + Fmt.I64Str (n) + ' keywords -> ' + out)
  END
EXCEPT
| Io.IOError :
    Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: cannot read or write ' + out) ; Io.Halt (1)
| IndexError :
    Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: no program name to find the repository by') ; Io.Halt (1)
| ValueRange :
    Io.WriteLine ('mkkeywords: a character past one byte') ; Io.Halt (1)
END MkKeywords.
